FACT:  Only somebody who has either finished with a tourist or somebody
who has seen some pretty big spoilers is going to even KNOW about the
PYEC.  FACT:  Anybody who can finish with a tourist knows what they are
doing.  FACT:  Anybody who has seen enough spoilers to know about the
PYEC also knows what they are doing.
FACT:  The game is already a bit too easy in the later stages for people
who know what they are doing.

Therefore, taking away the ability to wish for other classes' quest
artifacts isn't going to hurt the new nethack players out there, but it
will make the game harder for more knowledgable people.  This is a Good
Thing, I think.

Also, I never wish for artifacts anyway, except of those rare occasions
when I get an early wish and I feel like getting a good weapon instead
of gray dragon scale mail.  By the time I hit the castle, I still need
several pieces of armor and usually other assorted essentials (blessed
magic markers, spellbooks of magic mapping, rings of levitation, amulets
of life saving and bags of holding come to mind immediately).  There's
no need for the PYEC...it just makes things easier for heavily spoiled
people.

